# ===== The Fool (Unbound) =====
@loca FOOL_AWAKE_NAME 0 - The Fool: Awakening
@loca FOOL_AWAKE_DESC Strike different enemies with attacks within a single round to awaken the Aspect of Curiosity until combat ends. Each goal you reach awakens one more tier.<br><br>If fewer enemies stand when your turn begins than a goal asks for, strikes on any enemy count towards that goal instead.<br><br>Level 3: strike 3 different enemies to gain <LSTag Type="Passive" Tooltip="Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Fool_I">Wanderlust</LSTag>.<br><br>Level 7: strike 4 different enemies to also gain <LSTag Type="Passive" Tooltip="Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Fool_II">Restless Wind</LSTag>.<br><br>Level 12: strike 5 different enemies to awaken as the <LSTag Type="Passive" Tooltip="Arcana_Passive_Aspect_Fool_III">Aspect of Curiosity</LSTag>.
@loca FOOL_I_NAME Wanderlust
@loca FOOL_I_DESC Your <LSTag Tooltip="MovementSpeed">movement speed</LSTag> increases by [1], you can move without provoking <LSTag Tooltip="OpportunityAttack">Opportunity Attacks</LSTag>, and your unarmed attacks deal an additional [2].
@loca FOOL_II_NAME Restless Wind
@loca FOOL_II_DESC You have <LSTag Tooltip="Advantage">Advantage</LSTag> on Dexterity <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throws</LSTag> and an additional <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>. Once per turn, Zephyr Strike doesn't cost a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.
@loca FOOL_III_NAME Aspect of Curiosity
@loca FOOL_III_DESC Your Dexterity increases by [1] and you have another additional <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>. Once per round, the first attack against you misses.
@loca FOOL_AWAKENED_NAME 0 - The Fool
@loca FOOL_AWAKENED_DESC Awakened as the Aspect of Curiosity until combat ends.
@loca FOOL_TIER_I_NAME 0 - The Fool: Awakened I
@loca FOOL_TIER_I_DESC Wanderlust: Your <LSTag Tooltip="MovementSpeed">movement speed</LSTag> increases by [1], you can move without provoking <LSTag Tooltip="OpportunityAttack">Opportunity Attacks</LSTag>, and your unarmed attacks deal an additional [2].<br><br>Only active while not wearing armour or using a shield.
@loca FOOL_TIER_II_NAME 0 - The Fool: Awakened II
@loca FOOL_TIER_II_DESC Wanderlust: Your <LSTag Tooltip="MovementSpeed">movement speed</LSTag> increases by [1], you can move without provoking <LSTag Tooltip="OpportunityAttack">Opportunity Attacks</LSTag>, and your unarmed attacks deal an additional [2].<br><br>Restless Wind: You have <LSTag Tooltip="Advantage">Advantage</LSTag> on Dexterity <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throws</LSTag> and an additional <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>. Once per turn, Zephyr Strike doesn't cost a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.<br><br>Only active while not wearing armour or using a shield.
@loca FOOL_TIER_III_NAME 0 - The Fool: Awakened III
@loca FOOL_TIER_III_DESC Wanderlust: Your <LSTag Tooltip="MovementSpeed">movement speed</LSTag> increases by [1], you can move without provoking <LSTag Tooltip="OpportunityAttack">Opportunity Attacks</LSTag>, and your unarmed attacks deal an additional [2].<br><br>Restless Wind: You have <LSTag Tooltip="Advantage">Advantage</LSTag> on Dexterity <LSTag Tooltip="SavingThrow">Saving Throws</LSTag> and an additional <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>. Once per turn, Zephyr Strike doesn't cost a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.<br><br>Aspect of Curiosity: Your Dexterity increases by [3] and you have another additional <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>. Once per round, the first attack against you misses.<br><br>Only active while not wearing armour or using a shield.
@loca FOOL_PROGRESS_NAME Awakening Progress
@loca FOOL_PROGRESS_DESC Hits that count towards your next Awakening tier this round. Resets when your turn begins.
@loca h56bc27caga588g2b1agc487ge918b523cedf Zephyr Strike
@loca FOOL_ZEPHYR_NAME Restless Wind
@loca FOOL_ZEPHYR_DESC The next Zephyr Strike this turn doesn't cost a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.
@loca h1e5b5d84gf8fag7d7bgc878g960616bd7ae2 After making an unarmed attack or casting an Arcane spell, you can make a <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Arcana_Created_ZephyrStrike">Zephyr Strike</LSTag> as a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.
@loca WIND_RIPOSTE_NAME Wind Riposte
@loca WIND_RIPOSTE_DESC When an enemy's melee attack misses you while Wind Whispers is active, use your <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag> to strike back with an unarmed attack.
@loca FOOLS_LUCK_NAME Fool's Luck
@loca FOOLS_LUCK_DESC Once per round, the first attack against you misses.
@loca LEAP_NAME Leap of Faith
@loca LEAP_DESC Dash through the fray, striking every creature in your path with an unarmed attack that also deals [1].<br><br>Afterwards, you can make a <LSTag Type="Spell" Tooltip="Target_Arcana_Created_ZephyrStrike">Zephyr Strike</LSTag> as a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.
@loca EVASIVE_OPENING_NAME Opening
@loca EVASIVE_OPENING_DESC Has <LSTag Tooltip="Advantage">Advantage</LSTag> on the next unarmed <LSTag Tooltip="AttackRoll">Attack Roll</LSTag> this turn.
# textos existentes que mudam (versao +1 em todo lugar que os cita)
@loca hb2cbdec3g90c8g7e43g9d01g7c45f6af7a6a Jumping no longer requires a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="BonusActionPoint">bonus action</LSTag>.<br><br>Equipping armour or a shield ends this effect.
@loca hba599070gc262gfacfg3f31geafbde30b608 Focusing on avoiding attacks. <LSTag Tooltip="AttackRoll">Attack Rolls</LSTag> against you have <LSTag Tooltip="Disadvantage">Disadvantage</LSTag>. When a melee attack misses, strikes back with an unarmed attack as a <LSTag Type="ActionResource" Tooltip="ReactionActionPoint">reaction</LSTag>.<br><br>Equipping armour or a shield ends this effect.

